// The sketch pen [SPEC 15.3] as a specimen board — nine captioned tiles, one
// feature each. Corner modifiers (`chamfer` / `fillet`) and an even-odd
// `circle()` bore; `angle(deg, n)`'s bearing — 0 up, clockwise — walked round a
// hexagon in 60° steps, the sixth edge left to `close()`; the two-point
// `arc(dx, dy, r)` at its tightest legal radius, `r` exactly half the chord.
// Both readings of `mirror:`: an open subpath **fuses** end-to-end and generates
// its axis `|centerline|`, a closed one is **duplicated**. `pattern:`
// [SPEC 15.4] in both forms — `grid()` located by its first hole, `radial()` by
// the ring centre, which generates its `|pitch-circle|`. The line conventions
// [SPEC 15.7]: a dashed `|hidden|` cut, a manual `|centerline|` overhanging the
// profile, `stroke-style: phantom` for an alternate position. What repeats
// states once — `|view::drawing| { scale: 0.5 }` is the 1 : 2 ratio for all
// nine, `|arm::sketch|` the curve both positions wear — and `justify: end`
// bottoms every tile in its row, so the captions share a baseline. Lini's own
// wordmark drew this pen's first showcase; it lives in `logo.lini` now.
{
  layout: grid; columns: repeat(3); gap: 30 34; justify: end; padding: 30;

  |tile::column| { gap: 10; align: center; }
  |cap::block| { font-size: 12; color: --muted; }
  |view::drawing| { scale: 0.5; }
  |arm::sketch| {
    draw: move(-30, 8) right(16) curve(10, 0, 14, -14, 26, -16) right(18);
    fill: none;
  }
}

|tile| [
  |view| [
    |sketch#plate| {
      draw: move(0, 0) right(52) chamfer(9) down(30) left(52) fillet(9) close()
            move(26, 15) circle(7);
    }
  ]
  |cap| "chamfer · fillet · bore"
]

|tile| [
  |view| [
    |sketch#nut| {
      draw: move(-12, -20.78) angle(90, 24) angle(150, 24) angle(210, 24)
            angle(270, 24) angle(330, 24) close();
    }
  ]
  |cap| "angle — 0 up, clockwise"
]

|tile| [
  |view| [
    |sketch#slot| {
      draw: move(-16, -11) right(32) arc(0, 22, 11) left(32) arc(0, -22, 11)
            close();
    }
  ]
  |cap| "arc — the two-point form"
]

|tile| [
  |view| [
    // Draw the half, get the whole — and the axis centreline with it.
    |sketch#pin| {
      draw: move(-25, 0) up(9) right(20):collar down(4) right(30) down(5);
      mirror: x-axis;
    }
  ]
  |cap| "mirror — fused"
]

|tile| [
  |view| [
    // A closed subpath reflects as a second copy.
    |sketch#clip| {
      draw: move(-24, -10) right(16) down(20) left(16) close();
      mirror: y-axis;
    }
  ]
  |cap| "mirror — twinned"
]

|tile| [
  |view| [
    |sketch#strap| { draw: move(-30, -12) right(60) down(24) left(60) close(); } [
      |hole#bolt| { width: 8; translate: -21 0; pattern: grid(4, 1, 14, 0); }
    ]
  ]
  |cap| "pattern — grid"
]

|tile| [
  |view| [
    |sketch#flange| { draw: move(0, 0) circle(22) circle(7); } [
      |hole#bolt| { width: 6; pattern: radial(6, 14.5); }
    ]
  ]
  |cap| "pattern — radial"
]

|tile| [
  |view| [
    |sketch#body| { draw: move(-26, -14) right(52) down(28) left(52) close(); }
    |hidden#vee| { draw: move(-11, 14) line(11, -15) line(11, 15); }
    |centerline| { points: 0 -20, 0 20; }
  ]
  |cap| "hidden · centre line"
]

|tile| [
  |view| [
    |arm|
    |arm#raised| { translate: 0 -20; stroke-style: phantom; }
  ]
  |cap| "curve · alternate position"
]
